PROPOSED / NOT RATIFIED; materials only; not executed
Command: python3 -B score.py --oc

Operating characteristics of the per-arm rule "every one of the 6 rows has >= ceil(0.8 n) encoders on the key verdict".
p = per-encoder probability of giving the key verdict on a row, assumed equal and INDEPENDENT across encoders and rows
(both assumptions are optimistic; analysis-plan.md 3.5). P(row) = P(Bin(n,p) >= thr); P(arm) = P(row)^6.
